From: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kpatch-build: coalesce livepatch function text before conversion

Function sections are needed to identify changed functions, but retaining
them in the final livepatch module also creates one late relocation section
per function and target object. On x86 each such section causes a separate
text_poke_sync() all-CPU rendezvous when the target object is already loaded.

Coalesce ordinary function text during the existing module link, after diff
generation and before create-klp-module. The linker updates symbol values
and destination relocations, which create-klp-module already uses to derive
section-relative relocation offsets. Keep the saferet island separate, as
well as init, noinstr and all data sections. Leave the legacy kpatch backend
and non-x86 builds unchanged.

This reduces redundant rendezvous, not their safety requirements: the kernel
still validates and writes every relocation and synchronizes each resulting
object/section through its unchanged architecture implementation.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
---
 kmod/patch/kpatch.lds.S | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kmod/patch/kpatch.lds.S b/kmod/patch/kpatch.lds.S
--- a/kmod/patch/kpatch.lds.S
+++ b/kmod/patch/kpatch.lds.S
@@ -10,6 +10,17 @@
 SECTIONS
 {
+#if defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__KPATCH_MODULE__)
+  /* Preserve the independently aligned hardening island. */
+  .text.vpsadminos.saferet : {
+    *(.text.vpsadminos.saferet)
+  }
+  /* Diff generation is complete; share late relocation destinations. */
+  .text : {
+    *(.text .text.*)
+  }
+#endif
+
   .kpatch.system_states : SUBALIGN(__SIZEOF_POINTER__) {
     __kpatch_system_states = . ;
     KEEP(*(.kpatch.system_states))
     KEEP(*(.kpatch.system_states.sentinel))
